# Hybrid search notes

Neither method wins everywhere:
- vectors find paraphrases ("car won't start" ↔ "engine fails to turn over");
- keywords find exact tokens (error codes, function names, file names) that embeddings blur.

Reciprocal rank fusion: for each document, score = Σ over the lists of 1 / (60 + rank in that list). Uses ranks, not raw scores, so no calibration between BM25 scores and cosine similarities is needed. Documents found by both lists rise to the top.

Our rule: turn hybrid on only if the evaluation set shows a Recall@5 gain over vectors alone; otherwise keep the simpler path. Keyword-only is always the fallback when the model isn't loaded.
